15. Test Kubernetes DNS — important

Now let's verify the thing our Go applications will eventually depend on:

postgres:5432

Run a temporary shell Pod:

kubectl run dns-test \
  -n artifact-platform \
  --rm -it \
  --image=busybox:1.36 \
  --restart=Never \
  -- sh

Inside it:

nslookup postgres

You should get an address for the PostgreSQL Service.

Then:

nc -zv postgres 5432

You should get a successful connection.

Exit:

exit

This proves:

Pod
  │
  │ DNS query: postgres
  ▼
Kubernetes DNS
  │
  ▼
PostgreSQL Service
  │
  ▼
PostgreSQL Pod :5432

That is one of the most important Kubernetes mechanisms your applications will use.





